From 2ddd37cb01caa25cbf912ff84eff75113fc3a80c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:46:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] NetPass StreetPass relay to your own NetPass server (Build
 154)

With NetPass's system patches the SpotPass module (about every 15 minutes) and
cecd send the console's StreetPass outboxes to https://api.netpass.cafe/spr.
New setting "netpass_relay_url" (Configure > Network, "StreetPass relay
(NetPass)"; Android: Network settings): when set, e.g. to a LocalPass at
https://netpass.nintendo.local, those requests go there instead (https when
no scheme is given, path kept). Empty keeps the official NetPass server. It is
independent of the custom Nintendo server.

Every relay request now logs its answer: "StreetPass relay <url>: 200" at
Info, or "refused with <status>" at Warning, with the 3ds-netpass-msg and
x-spr-* reply headers and the start of the body, so a refusal can be read in
the log (the official server answered 403 on 8 Nov 2026).

Tests: IsNetPassRelayUrl / RedirectNetPassRelayUrl (92 assertions pass).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
